# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
# The binary, if someone builds it in place with `go build .`
/aiprobe
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test, benchmark and profiling output
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
cpu.prof
mem.prof
/testdata/tmp/

# Reports AIProbe writes into the working directory. These are per-run output, not
# source, and they contain file paths and excerpts from whatever session produced
# them — so they must never be committed by accident.
aiprobe-report.html
aiprobe-overview.html
aiprobe-demo.html
*.aiprobe.json

# Local scratch space. Anything here is a working note, not a deliverable.
/tmp/
/scratch/
# Source material and reading notes that informed the design but are not part of it.
# Nothing in the repository links here, so publishing it would only add clutter for a
# first-time reader. Delete the directory if you would rather it were gone entirely.
/ref/

# Browser-automation artefacts from local UI checks
.playwright-mcp/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/

# Go workspace files are per-developer, and committing one breaks everyone else's
# build by pointing at directories that only exist on one machine.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Dependency vendoring is not used; if someone runs `go mod vendor` locally, that is
# their business and not the repository's.
/vendor/

# Environment and credentials. AIProbe needs no API key, but a contributor's shell
# may still have one lying around.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Editors and IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# macOS, Windows, Linux desktop droppings
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.directory

# Agent working directories. AIProbe reads these formats but a checkout of the
# project should never contain one.
.claude/
.kiro/
.codex/
.aiprobe/

# Roadmap and changelog are kept as local working notes for now and deliberately
# not published, so they are ignored rather than committed. Remove these lines to
# start publishing them.
/ROADMAP.md
/ROADMAP.zh-CN.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/CHANGELOG.zh-CN.md
